             `## 3. The view builder - ``z2ui5_cl_ui5_view_builder``` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `The builder maps **any** UI5 XML view 1:1 - every control, property,` && |\n| &&
             `aggregation and namespace, nothing is wrapped or approximated. Four verbs:` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `| Verb | XML meaning | Tree action |` && |\n| &&
             `|---|---|---|` && |\n| &&
             `| ``ele( n ns )`` | opening tag ``<X>`` | add child and **descend** into it |` && |\n| &&
             `| ``tag( n ns )`` | self-closing ``<X/>`` | add child, **stay** on current node |` && |\n| &&
             `| ``end( )`` | closing ``</X>`` | **ascend** to the parent |` && |\n| &&
             `| ``a( n v )`` / ``a( n b )`` | one ``name="value"`` | attribute on the element the chain points at |` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `- ``n`` = tag name, ``ns`` = namespace **prefix** (``f``, ``l``, ``core``, ``mvc``, ...);` && |\n| &&
             `  omit ``ns`` for the default namespace (usually ``sap.m``). Declare every` && |\n| &&
             `  namespace as ``xmlns:*`` attributes on the root ``View``, exactly like XML.` && |\n| &&
             `- **Aggregations are just tags**: ``)->ele( ``items`` )`` for ``<items>``. An` && |\n| &&
             `  aggregation carries the same prefix as in the XML - ``<m:content>`` under a` && |\n| &&
             `  ``sap.ui.table`` default namespace is ``)->ele( n = ``content`` ns = ``m`` )``.` && |\n| &&
             `- ``stringify( )`` renders from the root, so trailing ``end( )`` calls before` && |\n| &&
             `  the final ``).`` are optional - ``end`` only moves the cursor to add siblings.` && |\n| &&
             `  That is also what lets the whole view hang off the ``factory( )`` in one` && |\n| &&
             `  statement (see "Formatting the chain" below).` && |\n| &&
             `- **Booleans from ABAP variables** go through ``b`` instead of ``v``:` && |\n| &&
             `  ```` )->a( n = ``editable`` b = mv_edit_mode ) ```` renders ``true``/``false`` (a` && |\n| &&
             `  literal is just ```` v = ``true`` ```` - never feed ``abap_true`` into ``v`` raw, it` && |\n| &&
             `  serializes as ``X``).` && |\n| &&
             `- **An element gets its attributes before its first child.** ``a( )`` lands on` && |\n| &&
             `  the element the chain is pointing at - the child just added by ``ele( )`` or` && |\n| &&
             `  ``tag( )``, or the node itself while it has none. Once an element has a` && |\n| &&
             `  child, ``a( )`` can no longer reach it.` && |\n| &&
             `- Braces ``{ }`` inside an ABAP ``|...|`` string template must be escaped` && |\n| &&
             `  ``\{ \}`` - an unescaped ``{`` is parsed as a UI5 binding.` && |\n| &&
             `- **Text from data goes through ``t``, not ``v``.** The same brace rule holds at` && |\n| &&
             `  runtime: the page runs with complex binding syntax, so a *value* that` && |\n| &&
             `  contains ``{``/``}`` - user input, an external payload - is parsed by UI5 as a` && |\n| &&
             `  binding (or expression) instead of shown as text, and can read arbitrary` && |\n| &&
             `  paths out of the view model. So a value that carries data is passed as` && |\n| &&
             `  ``t``, which the builder escapes as a literal:` && |\n| &&
             `  ```` )->a( n = ``title`` t = |Results for { mv_search }| ) ````.` && |\n| &&
             `  ``v`` stays the form for everything with binding vocabulary (``_bind``, an` && |\n| &&
             `  event, a ``{/path}`` template, an expression) and for constant text, which` && |\n| &&
             `  needs no escaping - never pass a deliberate binding as ``t``, escaping` && |\n| &&
             `  breaks it. Only the app knows which values are literals, which is why` && |\n| &&
             `  ``a( )`` does not decide it for ``v``. When ONE attribute mixes text with a` && |\n| &&
             `  binding, escape the text part yourself with` && |\n| &&
             `  ``z2ui5_cl_ui5_view_builder=>escape_literal( )`` inside ``v``. XML escaping is` && |\n| &&
             `  separate and always applied.` && |\n| &&
