             `  view->ele( ``Shell`` )->ele( ``Page`` ... ) ````, then ``page->ele( ... )`` per subtree,` && |\n| &&
             `  each its own statement, each starting at the method's indent. Every app in` && |\n| &&
             `  the framework and in ``abap2UI5/samples`` is built this way, and it is what` && |\n| &&
             `  keeps the rule above satisfiable: a statement that never unwinds can indent` && |\n| &&
             `  monotonically. A subtree deep enough that its lines drift past the` && |\n| &&
             `  right-hand side of the screen is telling you the same thing - split it.` && |\n| &&
             `- **A control's ``a( )`` lines sit one level (4 spaces) in from the control's` && |\n| &&
             `  own ``)->`` line** - one attribute per line, ``v =`` column aligned across the` && |\n| &&
             `  block.` && |\n| &&
             `- **A blank line opens a block - nothing else in the chain gets one.** A` && |\n| &&
             `  block is a run of lines that is read as one thing, and there are exactly` && |\n| &&
             `  two of them:` && |\n| &&
             `  1. **the content of a control that carries attributes** - a blank after its` && |\n| &&
             `     last ``a( )``, before its first child. The attribute lines are the` && |\n| &&
             `     control's own head; the content starts below them;` && |\n| &&
             `  2. **a run of ``tag``s** - a blank before the first one, none between them.` && |\n| &&
             `     A form's fields, a toolbar's buttons, a list's items belong together and` && |\n| &&
             `     are read as one block, whether or not each carries attributes.` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `  Everything else runs without a blank:` && |\n| &&
             `  - **none** between a control and its own ``a( )``s - they are its head, not` && |\n| &&
             `    its content;` && |\n| &&
             `  - **none between consecutive ``tag``s** - see block 2. This overrules` && |\n| &&
             `    "separate a sibling": only a *container* block is set off from the` && |\n| &&
             `    sibling before it;` && |\n| &&
             `  - **none** after a bare ``ele`` whose first child is another ``ele`` - a` && |\n| &&
             `    ``Shell`` -> ``Page`` scaffold is one path down, not two blocks;` && |\n| &&
             `  - **blank before every ``end``**; none after an ``end`` or between two ``end``s.` && |\n| &&
             `- Long text or binding values split with ``&&`` - an ``.abap`` line is capped at` && |\n| &&
             `  255 characters.` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `The two blocks, and the scaffold that is neither:` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             ```````abap` && |\n| &&
             `    )->ele( ``Shell``                        " bare ele into another ele -` && |\n| &&
             `        )->ele( ``Page``                     " one path down, no blank` && |\n| &&
             `            )->a( n = ``title`` v = ``My App``` && |\n| &&
             `                                           " block 1: Page's content starts` && |\n| &&
             `            )->ele( n = ``SimpleForm`` ns = ``form``` && |\n| &&
             `                )->a( n = ``editable`` v = ``true``` && |\n| &&
             `                                           " block 1: SimpleForm's content` && |\n| &&
             `                )->ele( n = ``content`` ns = ``form``` && |\n| &&
             `                                           " block 2: the run of leafs` && |\n| &&
             `                    )->tag( n = ``Title`` ns = ``core``` && |\n| &&
             `                        )->a( n = ``text``  v = ``Your data``` && |\n| &&
             `                    )->tag( ``Label``` && |\n| &&
             `                        )->a( n = ``text``  v = ``Name``` && |\n| &&
             `                    )->tag( ``Input``` && |\n| &&
             `                        )->a( n = ``value`` v = client->_bind( name ) ).` && |\n| &&
             ```````` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `The blank above ``Title`` is what makes the three fields read as the form's` && |\n| &&
             `content rather than as a continuation of the ``content`` aggregation; the` && |\n| &&
             `missing blanks between them are what keep the three together. Blanks in both` && |\n| &&
             `places, or in neither, and the same view reads as a pile of fragments.` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `**The blank lines are the part no gate catches.** abaplint's formatting rules` && |\n| &&
             `are deliberately kept off the app chains (``align_parameters`` and` && |\n| &&
             ```line_break_multiple_parameters`` are excluded in the framework repository's` && |\n| &&
             ```.github/abaplint/auto_abaplint_fix.jsonc``, and ``in_statement_indentation``` && |\n| &&
             `is excluded for the shipped apps - they would` && |\n| &&
             `flatten exactly the layout this section builds), and no linter rule judges` && |\n| &&
             `where a blank line belongs. That stays with the reader.` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `The *shape* around them is judged. The abap2UI5-linter has three layout rules:` && |\n| &&
             ```chain-indentation`` (a sibling in a different column than its siblings, a call` && |\n| &&
             `written left of the element it belongs to; the step *size* is not judged, only` && |\n| &&
             `that a chain keeps its own rhythm), ``chain-element-per-line`` (several controls` && |\n| &&
             `on one line; attributes may share their control's line, and so may the` && |\n| &&
             `container it opens), and ``chain-house-layout``, which judges the step size too` && |\n| &&
             `and is the one this section describes.` && |\n|.
    result = result &&
             |\n| &&
             `**All three default to ``hint``, which a config with ``failOn: warning`` does not` && |\n| &&
             `even print - so what decides is the repository you are in, and every repository` && |\n| &&
             `in this ecosystem raises them.** ``abap2UI5``, ``abap2UI5/samples-stack`` and` && |\n| &&
             ```abap2UI5/app-template`` enable ``chain-house-layout`` at ``warning``;` && |\n| &&
             ```abap2UI5/samples`` raises ``chain-indentation`` and ``chain-element-per-line``` && |\n| &&
             `instead; ``abap2UI5/samples-controls`` runs its own ``chain-format`` gate. Check` && |\n| &&
             `the config before you trust a green run - and either way, re-read the chain you` && |\n| &&
             `just wrote against the example above.` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `#### What a broken chain looks like` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `From ``abap2UI5/samples`` ``z2ui5_cl_smp_app_052``, after the port to this builder` && |\n| &&
             `- lint-green, and unreadable:` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             ```````abap` && |\n| &&
             `    lo_popover->ele( ``Popover``` && |\n| &&
             `        )->a( n = ``title``        v = |abap2UI5 - Popover - { mv_product }|` && |\n| &&
             `        )->a( n = ``contentWidth`` v = ``20rem`` )->ele( n = ``SimpleForm`` ns = ``form``` && |\n| &&
             `          )->a( n = ``layout``   v = ``ColumnLayout``` && |\n| &&
             `          )->a( n = ``editable`` b = abap_false )->ele( n = ``content`` ns = ``form`` )->tag( ``Label``` && |\n| &&
             `              )->a( n = ``text`` v = ``Product`` )->tag( ``Text``` && |\n| &&
             `              )->a( n = ``text`` v = mv_product )->tag( ``Text``` && |\n| &&
             `              )->a( n = ``text`` v = ``this is a text`` )->end( )->end( )->ele( ``footer`` )->ele( ``OverflowToolbar``` && |\n| &&
             `              )->tag( ``ToolbarSpacer`` )->tag( ``Button``` && |\n| &&
             `                )->a( n = ``press`` v = client->_event( ``BUTTON_DETAILS`` ) ).` && |\n| &&
             ```````` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `Three defects, and they compound: the indent steps by 2 and then by 4 and then` && |\n| &&
             `stops moving at all; one line opens ``content`` *and* a ``Label``; and the` && |\n| &&
             ````` )->end( )->end( )->ele( ``footer`` )->ele( ``OverflowToolbar`` ```` at the end of` && |\n| &&
             `an attribute line leaves the ``ToolbarSpacer`` two levels away from where its` && |\n| &&
             `column claims it is. Nothing here says ``footer`` is a sibling of ``SimpleForm``.` && |\n| &&
             `The same tree, with the subtree held in a variable:` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             ```````abap` && |\n| &&
             `    DATA(popover) = lo_popover->ele( ``Popover``` && |\n| &&
             `        )->a( n = ``title``        v = |abap2UI5 - Popover - { mv_product }|` && |\n| &&
             `        )->a( n = ``contentWidth`` v = ``20rem`` ).` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `    popover->ele( n = ``SimpleForm`` ns = ``form``` && |\n| &&
             `        )->a( n = ``layout``   v = ``ColumnLayout``` && |\n| &&
             `        )->a( n = ``editable`` b = abap_false` && |\n| &&
             `        )->ele( n = ``content`` ns = ``form``` && |\n| &&
             `            )->tag( ``Label`` )->a( n = ``text`` v = ``Product``` && |\n| &&
             `            )->tag( ``Text``  )->a( n = ``text`` v = mv_product` && |\n| &&
             `            )->tag( ``Text``  )->a( n = ``text`` v = ``this is a text`` ).` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `    popover->ele( ``footer`` )->ele( ``OverflowToolbar``` && |\n| &&
             `        )->tag( ``ToolbarSpacer``` && |\n| &&
             `        )->tag( ``Button``` && |\n| &&
             `            )->a( n = ``press`` v = client->_event( ``BUTTON_DETAILS`` )` && |\n| &&
             `            )->a( n = ``text``  v = ``details`` ).` && |\n| &&
             ```````` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `## 4. Data binding` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `- ``client->_bind( var )`` binds a PUBLIC attribute: the value renders into` && |\n| &&
             `  the view, and user input is written back into the attribute` && |\n| &&
             `  before your event handler runs. Use it for everything, display-only` && |\n| &&
             `  included (``_bind_edit`` is an obsolete alias - do not use it in new code).` && |\n| &&
             `- Inside a bound aggregation (a table/list template), child properties bind` && |\n| &&
             `  **relative to the row** with braces on the upper-cased field name:` && |\n| &&
             `  ```` ``{PRODUCT}`` ````. A camelCase ABAP field ``supplierName`` becomes` && |\n| &&
             `  ``{SUPPLIERNAME}``.` && |\n| &&
             `- A value shared by the whole app lives at the model **root** - inside a row` && |\n| &&
             `  template a relative ``{FIELD}`` resolves against the row and silently renders` && |\n| &&
             `  empty if the row has no such column; bind root values with` && |\n| &&
             `  ``client->_bind( field )`` even inside templates.` && |\n| &&
             `- **Never hard-code a model path as text** (``'/T_ITEMS'``): paths come from` && |\n| &&
             `  ``_bind``, so renames cannot break bindings. For raw binding-info strings` && |\n| &&
             `  (typed bindings, sorters) get the bare path via` && |\n| &&
             `  ``client->_bind( val = t_items path = abap_true )``, e.g.` && |\n| &&
             `  ```` v = |\{ path: '{ client->_bind( val = t_items path = abap_true ) }', sorter: \{ path: 'PRODUCT' \} \}| ````` &&
             `.` && |\n| &&
             `- Typed/complex bindings pass through verbatim (braces escaped):` && |\n| &&
             `  ```` v = |\{ path: 'PRICE', type: 'sap.ui.model.type.Float' \}| ```` - note the` && |\n| &&
             `  ``path:`` uses the upper-cased ABAP field name.` && |\n| &&
             `- Type numeric/boolean model fields as ``i``/``p``/``abap_bool``, not ``string`` -` && |\n| &&
             `  UI5 2.x rejects a JSON string on a float/int/boolean control property.` && |\n| &&
             `- An ABAP field is never *absent* - it is initial - so by default every field` && |\n| &&
             `  reaches the browser as an explicit ``""``/``0``, which **overrides the control's` && |\n| &&
             `  own default** (and an enum-typed property rejects the empty string outright).` && |\n| &&
             `  When a bound template's rows fill different subsets of the same properties,` && |\n| &&
             `  bind with ``client->_bind( val = t_rows omit_initial = abap_true )``: initial` && |\n| &&
             `  fields then stay out of the model and each control keeps its UI5 default.` && |\n| &&
             `  A **boolean that must send ``false``** is the exception - ``abap_false`` is` && |\n| &&
             `  itself initial, so the blanket flag would drop it and the control would fall` && |\n| &&
             `  back to its default ``true``. Scope the omission instead:` && |\n| &&
             `  ``client->_bind( val = t_rows omit_initial_paths = VALUE #( ( ``MIN`` ) ( ``MAX`` ) ) )``` && |\n| &&
             `  lists the columns that may vanish and leaves every other field alone.` && |\n| &&
             `- A control property that expects an **object** - a ``sap.ui.integration``` && |\n| &&
             `  widgets:Card ``manifest`` is the case this exists for - cannot be fed from a` && |\n| &&
             `  typed ABAP value at all: a manifest's keys (``sap.app``, ``sap.card``) are not` && |\n| &&
             `  valid ABAP field names, so it is no structure, and UI5 reads a *string*` && |\n| &&
             `  manifest as a manifest **URL**. Keep the JSON in a ``string`` attribute and` && |\n| &&
             `  bind it with ``client->_bind( val = manifest json = abap_true )`` - the` && |\n| &&
             `  serializer then splices its content into the model as a JSON node instead of` && |\n| &&
             `  a quoted string. Outbound only (the client renders such a payload, it never` && |\n| &&
             `  authors it), and a string that does not parse raises rather than shipping` && |\n| &&
             `  broken JSON. Where the sample keeps one manifest per file, bind its URL` && |\n| &&
             `  instead - that path needs no flag.` && |\n| &&
             `- **Bound data changed in an event handler is pushed automatically** - the` && |\n| &&
             `  framework compares the model before and after ``main( )`` on every event` && |\n| &&
             `  round-trip and, when it differs, sends it to every open view slot (MAIN,` && |\n| &&
             `  POPUP, POPOVER; the nested views inherit MAIN's model). A handler cannot` && |\n| &&
             `  render stale by forgetting anything: there is nothing to call and nothing` && |\n| &&
             `  to switch on. Call ``view_display`` again only when the view **structure**` && |\n| &&
             `  itself changes.` && |\n| &&
             `- ``view_model_update( )``, ``popup_model_update( )``, ``popover_model_update( )``` && |\n| &&
             `  and the two nested variants are **obsolete and do nothing**. They stay in` && |\n| &&
             `  the interface so existing apps keep compiling; delete the calls whenever` && |\n| &&
             `  you touch such an app, and never add a new one.` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `## 5. Events` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `- Wire: ``)->a( n = ``press`` v = client->_event( ``SAVE`` ) )``.` && |\n| &&
             `- Read in ``on_event`` via ``CASE client->get_event( ).``.` && |\n| &&
             `- **Pass values into an event** with ``t_arg``; read them back with` && |\n| &&
             `  ``client->get_event_arg( )`` (index only for position 2+). A value resolved` && |\n| &&
             `  on the client must be ``$``-prefixed - ```` ``${PRODUCT}`` ```` (row field),` && |\n| &&
             `  ```` ``$event.oSource.sId`` ```` (the pressed control's id),` && |\n| &&
             `  ```` ``${$parameters>/selected}`` ```` (an event parameter). A bare ``{...}`` arg is` && |\n| &&
             `  NOT resolved and arrives empty. Booleans arrive as ``abap_bool`` (``X``/space).` && |\n| &&
             `- **A control-valued event parameter arrives as JSON.** Several UI5 events` && |\n| &&
             `  hand over a control or a whole array of controls rather than a scalar -` && |\n| &&
             `  ``ViewSettingsDialog.confirm`` gives ``filterItems``,` && |\n| &&
             `  ``SinglePlanningCalendar.selectedDatesChange`` a list of ``DateRange``. Pass the` && |\n| &&
             `  parameter like any other (```` ``${$parameters>/filterItems}`` ````); the frontend` && |\n| &&
             `  marshals each control into an object carrying its ``ID`` plus its public` && |\n| &&
             `  properties, so ``client->get_event_arg( )`` returns a JSON array. Read the one` && |\n| &&
             `  property you need out of it BY HAND, per the bullet below - not with` && |\n| &&
             `  ``z2ui5_cl_ajson``, which is framework-internal. Do **not** parse a display` && |\n| &&
             `  string such as ``filterString`` - it is localized and its format is not a` && |\n| &&
             `  contract.` && |\n| &&
             `  **Read only the fields you need**, and never expect the payload to be the` && |\n| &&
             `  shape you modelled: it carries *every* public property of the control - a` && |\n| &&
             `  ``ViewSettingsItem`` also brings ``enabled``, ``textDirection`` and ``wrapping`` -` && |\n| &&
             `  so a reader that walks for one named key is both the smallest and the most` && |\n| &&
             `  robust thing to write. Two properties on the same object need two walks,` && |\n| &&
             `  which is still less code than a mapping that has to anticipate the rest.` && |\n| &&
             `  **Not every such payload is flat.** ``projectValue`` in` && |\n| &&
             `  ``app/webapp/core/Lib.js`` passes an object- or array-valued property through` && |\n| &&
             `  unchanged (up to ``MAX_ARG_DEPTH``), so a control with a property typed` && |\n| &&
             `  ``object``/``any`` marshals as a nested node. When that is what you are looking` && |\n| &&
             `  at, do not grow the reader: bind the value into the model instead and let` && |\n| &&
             `  the framework's own write-back fill the ABAP structure - ``whole_value_apply``` && |\n| &&
             `  in ``z2ui5_cl_ui5_srv_model`` converts a whole object or array with` && |\n| &&
             `  ``to_abap( iv_corresponding = abap_true )``, which is the corresponding-only` && |\n| &&
             `  mapping this used to reach ajson for, already written and already released.` && |\n| &&
             `- **JSON is built and read BY HAND, and there is no released parser.**` && |\n| &&
             `  ``z2ui5_cl_ui5_json`` was one for two weeks and was removed on 2026-09-14,` && |\n| &&
             `  before it had shipped in any release - nothing downstream lost it, and` && |\n| &&
             `  nothing has to be migrated. Do not reach for a substitute: ``/ui2/cl_json``` && |\n| &&
             `  is not released for ABAP Cloud, ``xco_cp_json`` is missing on 7.02, and the` && |\n| &&
             `  vendored ajson is framework-internal, which the linter's` && |\n| &&
             `  ``non-released-api`` rule reports - correctly.` && |\n| &&
             `  - **Outbound** (a control property that must receive an OBJECT, e.g. a` && |\n| &&
             `    ``sap.ui.integration`` Card manifest): compose the JSON as a string in` && |\n| &&
             `    ABAP and bind it with ``_bind( val = ... json = abap_true )``, which splices` && |\n| &&
             `    it in as a model node instead of a quoted string.` && |\n| &&
             `  - **Inbound** (an event argument that arrives as JSON): write the few` && |\n| &&
             `    lines that read the one field you need. Where the payload is written by` && |\n| &&
             `    the framework and flat, a targeted ``find``/``substring_before`` walk is the` && |\n| &&
             `    whole job - ``z2ui5_cl_smp_app_197`` (``json_get_values``, one property` && |\n| &&
             `    across an array of objects) and ``z2ui5_cl_smp_app_327`` (``json_get_value``,` && |\n| &&
             `    one field of a flat object) in ``abap2UI5/samples`` are the pattern to copy.` && |\n| &&
             `    Two cases need more than that, and both have an answer that is not a` && |\n| &&
             `    bigger parser:` && |\n| &&
             `    - **The payload is NESTED** (see the control-parameter bullet above):` && |\n| &&
             `      bind the value instead of parsing the event argument. A two-way bound` && |\n| &&
             `      attribute is filled by the framework's own write-back, corresponding` && |\n| &&
             `      fields only, with no app-side parsing at all.` && |\n| &&
             `    - **The app WROTE the payload itself** - publishing into an AMC channel,` && |\n| &&
             `      writing browser storage - so it carries free user input. Then escaping` && |\n| &&
             `      is the job: a quote the user typed reaches the reader as ``\"``, and a` && |\n| &&
             `      ``substring_before`` on the next quote ends the value early. Escape on` && |\n| &&
             `      the way out and WALK the value on the way in, resolving escapes;` && |\n| &&
             `      ``z2ui5_cl_smps_app_489`` in ``abap2UI5/samples-stack`` (``json_build``,` && |\n| &&
             `      ``json_escape``, ``json_get_string``) is that case written out. The walk` && |\n| &&
             `      also makes the key search safe: text containing ``","author":"`` cannot` && |\n| &&
             `      forge a sibling field, because its quotes are escaped and no longer` && |\n| &&
             `      match the marker.` && |\n| &&
             `    An app parsing genuinely arbitrary, nested JSON is doing something this` && |\n| &&
             `    framework does not hand it a tool for.` && |\n| &&
             `- **A dynamic type names a type the SYSTEM has, not one abap2UI5 ships.**` && |\n| &&
             `  ``CREATE DATA ... TYPE STANDARD TABLE OF (name)`` needs a name that exists at` && |\n| &&
             `  runtime, and the name belongs to the app's own domain - a DDIC structure of` && |\n| &&
             `  the customer's, a CDS view, whatever the app is browsing. The framework` && |\n| &&
             `  released ``z2ui5_t_02`` (a ``name``/``value`` pair) as an anchor for exactly this` && |\n| &&
             `  and **removed it again on 2026-09-22**: in a year not one sample, and no app` && |\n| &&
             `  anybody reported, ever named it. abap2UI5 adds no dictionary object an app` && |\n| &&
             `  is supposed to point at (section  *No new dictionary objects* in ``AGENTS.md``), and` && |\n| &&
             `  the framework's own tables (``z2ui5_t_01``) are internals that may change -` && |\n| &&
             `  naming one from an app is borrowing a table, not using an API.` && |\n| &&
             `- **The per-wire flags (``s_ctrl``, type ``ty_s_event_control``).** By default` && |\n| &&
             `  an event fired while a roundtrip is in flight is DROPPED - right for a` && |\n| &&
             `  click, wrong for a per-keystroke wire (``liveChange``, ``liveSearch``,` && |\n| &&
             `  ``sliderChange``), where it loses every keystroke typed under the running` && |\n| &&
             `  roundtrip, the last one included, and leaves the backend at the value of` && |\n| &&
             `  the last completed roundtrip while the control shows the current one.` && |\n| &&
             `  ``check_queue_last = abap_true`` keeps the LAST event fired on the wire and` && |\n| &&
             `  dispatches it once the response has landed - one roundtrip in flight at a` && |\n| &&
             `  time, order preserved, the backend ends on the control's current value;` && |\n| &&
             `  no debounce, so a pause still costs one roundtrip. Pair it with` && |\n| &&
             `  ``check_no_busy = abap_true``, which keeps the full-screen busy overlay` && |\n| &&
             `  down for that wire - without it every keystroke landing on a roundtrip in` && |\n| &&
             `  flight raises the overlay at once, over the very field being typed into` && |\n| &&
             `  (the roundtrip, the busy STATE and the guard are unchanged, only the` && |\n| &&
             `  overlay is not shown). There is no flag for` && |\n| &&
             `  sending every firing at once: only the newest response may commit, so the` && |\n| &&
             `  earlier roundtrips would be work thrown away. A background wire that must` && |\n| &&
             `  not wait - a timer tick, a poll - needs no queue flag either: ``START_TIMER``` && |\n| &&
             `  carries its own slot and waits out the roundtrip in flight` && |\n| &&
             `  (``core/actions/ViewOps.js``, ``evStartTimer``). What it does share with a` && |\n| &&
             `  click is the overlay: a tick raises it after the usual one-second delay,` && |\n| &&
             `  so a poll whose backend call takes longer flashes it over a screen nobody` && |\n| &&
             `  is waiting on. An optional third ``t_arg``, ```` ``X`` ```` - ``abap_true`` as` && |\n| &&
             `  ``t_arg`` spells every flag - is the tick's ``check_no_busy``:` && |\n| &&
             `  ```` client->follow_up_action( val = z2ui5_if_client=>cs_event-start_timer t_arg = VALUE #( ( ``TICK`` ) ( ``5000` &&
             ``` ) ( ``X`` ) ) ) ````.` && |\n| &&
             `  Like the flag, it takes the overlay down and nothing else - a click that` && |\n| &&
             `  lands while the tick is in flight is still dropped, and still raises it.` && |\n| &&
             `  ``check_prevent_default`` / ``prevent_default_expr`` cancel the` && |\n| &&
             `  control's built-in default before the roundtrip, ``check_arg_literal``` && |\n| &&
             `  quotes every argument - see the doc on ``z2ui5_if_client=>_event``.` && |\n| &&
             `- Roundtrip-free client actions: ``client->follow_up_action( val = ... t_arg = ... )``` && |\n| &&
             `  written where its RESULT is consumed - in a view attribute - runs a` && |\n| &&
             `  whitelisted frontend action without a server call (toast from a row value,` && |\n| &&
             `  client-side sort/filter via ``binding_call``, ...). ``client->_event_client( )``` && |\n| &&
             `  is the obsolete name for exactly this and emits the identical wire.` && |\n| &&
             `- After the response, ``client->follow_up_action( val = ... t_arg = ... )`` as a` && |\n| &&
             `  STATEMENT schedules a frontend action: focus (``cs_event-set_focus``), scroll, title,` && |\n| &&
             `  clipboard, timers, keyboard shortcuts, ``control_by_id`` (call a public` && |\n| &&
             `  method on a control), ``binding_call`` (filter/sort an aggregation binding).` && |\n| &&
             `  The full catalog with per-action ``t_arg`` documentation sits on` && |\n| &&
             `  ``z2ui5_if_client=>follow_up_action`` and in ``cs_event``.` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `## 6. Popups, popovers, messages` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `- ``client->popup_display( val = ... )`` opens a ``core:FragmentDefinition``` && |\n| &&
             `  string (build it with ``z2ui5_cl_ui5_view_builder`` too) as a dialog. Closing: wire a` && |\n| &&
             `  Close button to ``client->follow_up_action( val = z2ui5_if_client=>cs_event-popup_close )``` && |\n| &&
             `  (round-trip free - the frontend tears the popup slot down without reaching` && |\n| &&
             `  your ``main``), or call ``client->popup_destroy( )`` server-side after handling` && |\n| &&
             `  your own event. Not ``_event( cs_event-popup_close )``: that is a backend` && |\n| &&
             `  event named ``POPUP_CLOSE`` like any other, it reaches ``main( )`` and closes` && |\n| &&
             `  nothing by itself.` && |\n| &&
             `- ``client->popover_display( xml = ... by_id = ... )`` anchors a popover to a` && |\n| &&
             `  control id. **Mind the asymmetry**: the popup takes its XML as ``val``, the` && |\n| &&
             `  popover as ``xml`` - one of the most common first-try mistakes.` && |\n| &&
             `- ``client->message_toast_display( text )`` and` && |\n| &&
             `  ``client->message_box_display( text type title actions ... )`` for messages -` && |\n| &&
             `  never build your own toast/dialog for these.` && |\n| &&
             `- **``message_box_display( text )`` takes anything.** ``text`` is ``TYPE any``, so` && |\n| &&
             `  throw in what you have: a string, a BAPIRET2 / T100 / RAP / ``symsg``` && |\n| &&
             `  structure or table, a log object, an exception, an HTML string, a business` && |\n| &&
             `  table, a nested structure or tree, an object, a number. Messages are` && |\n| &&
             `  recognized first - they set the box's severity and title themselves and` && |\n| &&
             `  several of them collapse into one box with a bullet list. Anything else is` && |\n| &&
             `  rendered generically: a headline in the box (``Table with 12 entries``), the` && |\n| &&
             `  data itself in the details - which abap2UI5 shows unfolded, so nothing of it` && |\n| &&
             `  hides behind sap.m.MessageBox's "Show details" link. You do not pre-format` && |\n| &&
             `  anything and you do not branch on what you have. The one case that shows no` && |\n| &&
             `  box at all is complex data that is initial, so` && |\n| &&
             `  ``message_box_display( lt_return )`` after a call that returned nothing stays` && |\n| &&
             `  silent, as it always has. The sample ``Z2UI5_CL_SMP_APP_502`` in` && |\n| &&
             `  [abap2UI5/samples](https://github.com/abap2UI5/samples) walks every one of` && |\n| &&
             `  those cases with one button each.` && |\n| &&
             `- **A pure UI5 option is not a parameter of those two methods.** They carry` && |\n| &&
             `  what an ABAP app decides - the data, the kind of box, the buttons as a` && |\n| &&
             `  table, the backend event raised when it closes. Where a toast docks, how` && |\n| &&
             `  wide a box is, which icon it carries, what it is a dependent of: that is` && |\n| &&
             `  the control, and it is set through the whitelisted global call, whose last` && |\n| &&
             `  argument is the ``sap.m.MessageToast.show( )`` / ``sap.m.MessageBox.<type>( )``` && |\n| &&
             `  option object 1:1 (the display method IS the box type there, and a ``t_arg``` && |\n| &&
             `  starting with a brace travels as real JSON):` && |\n| &&
             `  ``client->follow_up_action( val = z2ui5_if_client=>cs_event-control_global t_arg =` && |\n| &&
             `  VALUE #( ( ``MESSAGE_BOX`` ) ( ``error`` ) ( ``Not saved.`` ) ( ``{"contentWidth":"30rem","icon":"WARNING"}`` ) ) )``` &&
             `.` && |\n| &&
             `  ``Z2UI5_CL_SMP_APP_381`` and ``Z2UI5_CL_SMP_APP_512`` are the two samples that` && |\n| &&
             `  show that half. Wired into a view the same call runs without a round-trip` && |\n| &&
             `  at all, and extra arguments fill ``{0}``, ``{1}`` placeholders in the text.` && |\n| &&
             `- Bind popup data exactly like main-view data; changed bound data reaches` && |\n| &&
             `  an open popup automatically.` && |\n| &&
             `- A popup or popover is closed automatically by anything that replaces the` && |\n| &&
             `  screen underneath it: a ``client->view_display( )`` in the same roundtrip` && |\n| &&
             `  and a navigation to another app both take it down. Re-open it in that same` && |\n| &&
             `  roundtrip if it is meant to stay - ``view_display( )`` first, then` && |\n| &&
             `  ``popup_display( )`` - and call ``popup_destroy( )`` only when you close it` && |\n| &&
             `  without rebuilding the view.` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `## 7. Multi-view, navigation, routing` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `- One app can render ``main``, two nested views, a popup and a popover` && |\n| &&
             `  simultaneously (``cs_view`` names them for scoped actions).` && |\n| &&
             `- Call another app: ``client->nav_app_call( NEW zcl_other_app( ) )``; return` && |\n| &&
             `  with ``client->nav_app_leave( )`` (or ``client->get_app_prev( )`` to hand data` && |\n| &&
             `  back). The framework keeps the app stack across roundtrips.` && |\n| &&
             `- URL routing: ``client->follow_up_action( val = z2ui5_if_client=>cs_event-hash_routing )``` && |\n| &&
             `  in ``check_on_init`` makes the app bookmarkable and wires the browser` && |\n| &&
             `  Back/Forward buttons - the mode rides in ``t_arg``: ``cs_nav_mode-keep`` (the` && |\n| &&
             `  default when ``t_arg`` is empty) restores the exact draft state,` && |\n| &&
             `  ``cs_nav_mode-fresh`` restarts clean. Works inside the Fiori Launchpad.` && |\n| &&
             `- The URL hash and the app state have named APIs of their own:` && |\n| &&
             `  ``client->hash_set( val )`` writes ``val`` as the app's URL hash with a pushed` && |\n| &&
             `  history entry (the UI5 router's ``navTo``), ``client->hash_replace( val )``` && |\n| &&
             `  writes it without one (``navTo( ..., true )`` - e.g. a layout arrow whose` && |\n| &&
             `  drags must not become Back steps). ``client->app_state_set_active( )``` && |\n| &&
             `  keeps the id of the CURRENT app state in the URL on every roundtrip, so a` && |\n| &&
             `  reload/bookmark/shared link restores the exact state;` && |\n| &&
             `  ``client->app_state_get_href( )`` returns the absolute, FLP-safe link to` && |\n| &&
             `  that state for the app to copy, show, mail or render as a QR code.` && |\n| &&
             `  The matching ``cs_event`` constants for ``follow_up_action( )`` wires:` && |\n| &&
             `  ``hash_set`` / ``hash_replace`` (the same two writes as frontend actions),` && |\n| &&
             `  ``hash_back`` (one history step back with an optional fallback hash),` && |\n| &&
             `  ``hash_attach_changed`` (registers a backend event that fires when the hash` && |\n| &&
             `  changes under the app - Back/Forward, a manual edit; app-owned routing` && |\n| &&
             `  with ``hash_routing`` off), ``hash_routing`` (the routing modes above) and` && |\n| &&
             `  ``app_state_set_active``. ``hash_routing``, ``hash_attach_changed`` and` && |\n| &&
             `  ``app_state_set_active`` are mutually exclusive - each claims the whole app` && |\n| &&
             `  hash.` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `## 8. Rules that keep apps portable` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `- **Thin frontend**: business logic (thresholds, classification, unit` && |\n| &&
             `  conversion, validation) is computed in ABAP and bound as a finished value -` && |\n| &&
             `  never in a frontend formatter or custom JS. The shipped ``z2ui5/model/formatter``` && |\n| &&
             `  helpers are a **marshalling layer, not a formatting toolbox**: a function` && |\n| &&
             `  only lives there when ABAP physically cannot produce the finished value -` && |\n| &&
             `  a real JS ``Date`` for an object-typed property (``DateCreateObject``,` && |\n| &&
             `  ``DateAbapDateToDateObject``, ``DateAbapDateTimeToDateObject``) or an icon-font` && |\n| &&
             `  glyph of the loaded theme (``expandInlineIcons``). That is the whole set.` && |\n| &&
             `  Rounding a number, joining fields into a string or mapping a status to a` && |\n| &&
             `  ``ValueState``/icon is your app's job: compute it in ABAP and bind it` && |\n| &&
             `  (``state="{STATUS_STATE}"``). Functions that did those things were shipped` && |\n| &&
             `  once and removed again - the module header states the admission criteria` && |\n| &&
             `  and ``npm run check:formatter`` enforces them.` && |\n| &&
             `- **UI5 1.71 floor**: the framework supports OpenUI5 down to 1.71. Before` && |\n| &&
             `  using a control/property/aggregation, check its "available since" in the` && |\n| &&
             `  UI5 API - post-1.71 members need a UI5 release that has them; a wrong` && |\n| &&
             `  aggregation name 404s the whole view on old releases.` && |\n| &&
             `- **State discipline**: every PUBLIC attribute is serialized into the draft` && |\n| &&
             `  and sent to the browser on every render. Large helper data, catalogs and` && |\n| &&
             `  anything not bound belongs in PROTECTED (or is re-read per request) - a` && |\n| &&
             `  bloated public section makes every click slower.` && |\n| &&
             `- Authorization is **the app's job**: any user who can reach the ICF node can` && |\n| &&
             `  start any ``z2ui5_if_app`` class. The framework performs no ``AUTHORITY-CHECK``` && |\n| &&
             `  of its own, on purpose ([security model](../security.md#what-the-app-has-to-do)).` && |\n| &&
             `  Check your authorizations at the top of ``main``, before any dispatch, and` && |\n| &&
             `  render an error when denied - the same place a transaction or a report` && |\n| &&
             `  does it. The shipped Hello World has no check because it guards nothing;` && |\n| &&
             `  an app that reads or writes business data starts like this:` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `  ``````abap` && |\n| &&
             `  METHOD z2ui5_if_app~main.` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `    AUTHORITY-CHECK OBJECT 'Z_MY_APP' ID 'ACTVT' FIELD '03'.` && |\n| &&
             `    IF sy-subrc <> 0.` && |\n| &&
             `      client->message_box_display( text = ``You are not authorized to use this app``` && |\n| &&
             `                                   type = ``error`` ).` && |\n| &&
             `      RETURN.` && |\n| &&
             `    ENDIF.` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `    me->client = client.` && |\n| &&
             `    IF client->check_on_init( ).` && |\n| &&
             `    ...` && |\n| &&
             `  ``````` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `  The check runs on every roundtrip, which is what you want: a revoked` && |\n| &&
             `  authorization takes effect on the next click, not on the next cold start.` && |\n| &&
             `- The default UI5 bootstrap loads from the CDN; system-local hosting and` && |\n| &&
             `  CSP/theme/bootstrap customizing go through ``z2ui5_if_ui5_exit`` /` && |\n| &&
             `  ``z2ui5_cl_ui5_user_exit``.` && |\n| &&
             `- **A third-party JS library is a deployment decision, not a view trick.**` && |\n| &&
             `  The default CSP in ``z2ui5_cl_ui5_user_exit`` allows script only from the` && |\n| &&
             `  UI5 CDN hosts (``ui5.sap.com``, ``sapui5.hana.ondemand.com``,` && |\n| &&
             `  ``openui5.hana.ondemand.com``, ``sdk.openui5.org``) - general-purpose CDNs` && |\n| &&
             `  such as ``cdn.jsdelivr.net`` and ``cdnjs.cloudflare.com`` are deliberately` && |\n| &&
             `  NOT on it. Every other host needs your own` && |\n| &&
             `  ``content_security_policy`` in the exit, and a system-local copy served by` && |\n| &&
             `  your own ICF node is the option that survives an offline system. Whichever` && |\n| &&
             `  you pick, load the library through the UI5 loader` && |\n| &&
             `  (``sap.ui.loader.config`` path mapping + ``sap.ui.define``) and drive it from a` && |\n| &&
             `  custom control; do **not** rely on the jQuery ``$`` global - UI5 2.x no` && |\n| &&
             `  longer ships it - and keep the library call itself free of business` && |\n| &&
             `  decisions (see "thin frontend" above).` && |\n| &&
             `- **An imperative UI5 method that has no bindable equivalent** - the` && |\n| &&
             `  ``sap.m.p13n.*`` panels take their item list only through ``setP13nData( )``,` && |\n| &&
             `  a ``sap.m.Carousel`` only moves via ``setActivePage( )`` - is reached with` && |\n| &&
             `  ``client->follow_up_action( val = cs_event-control_by_id ... )``. Check` && |\n| &&
             `  ``cs_event`` and the whitelist before writing custom JS: an argument the` && |\n| &&
             `  whitelist does not declare is silently dropped, but a method it declares` && |\n| &&
             `  needs no JS at all.` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `## 9. Validate and iterate like the framework does` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `- **Starting a new app repo? Use` && |\n| &&
             `  [abap2UI5/app-template](https://github.com/abap2UI5/app-template)** - it` && |\n| &&
             `  ships the starter app, abaplint + linter CI, this guide as its AGENTS.md` && |\n| &&
             `  and the agent permission setup preconfigured.` && |\n| &&
             `- **[abap2UI5-linter](https://github.com/abap2UI5/linter)** checks` && |\n| &&
             `  app classes statically (unknown/deprecated/too-new controls and members,` && |\n|.
    result = result &&
             `  binding mistakes, builder-tree defects) and can render the view headless:` && |\n| &&
             `  ``npx --yes @abap2ui5/linter my_app.clas.abap`` - also` && |\n| &&
             `  available as a GitHub Action and inside the VS Code extension.` && |\n| &&
             `- **[mcp-server](https://github.com/abap2UI5/mcp-server)** gives MCP-capable agents` && |\n| &&
             `  the full loop without a SAP system: ``capabilities`` -> ``deploy_app`` ->` && |\n| &&
             `  ``build_backend`` -> ``run_app`` (headless screenshot + errors).` && |\n| &&
             `- **[vscode-extension](https://github.com/abap2UI5/vscode-extension)**:` && |\n| &&
             `  F9 launches the class in an embedded preview against a real system.` && |\n| &&
             `- **Worked examples**, three catalogues with the same row shape, so one search` && |\n| &&
             `  reads all of them: curated apps for "has somebody built this pattern" in` && |\n| &&
             `  [abap2UI5/samples](https://github.com/abap2UI5/samples), 622 gate-verified` && |\n| &&
             `  demo-kit ports for "how is this control expressed" in` && |\n| &&
             `  [samples-controls](https://github.com/abap2UI5/samples-controls) (``src/``), and` && |\n| &&
             `  apps that need something from your stack - OData, RAP, APC, the launchpad -` && |\n| &&
             `  in [samples-stack](https://github.com/abap2UI5/samples-stack). What abap2UI5` && |\n| &&
             `  can express at all is answered in samples-controls' ``CAPABILITIES.md``, each` && |\n| &&
             `  claim naming the port that proves it.` && |\n| &&
             `- **Unit-test the app class without a system**: a local test double` && |\n| &&
             `  ``ltd_client`` with ``INTERFACES z2ui5_if_client PARTIALLY IMPLEMENTED.`` in` && |\n| &&
             `  the class's ``.clas.testclasses.abap`` answers ``check_on_init`` /` && |\n| &&
             `  ``check_on_event`` / ``get_event`` from attributes and records what` && |\n| &&
             `  ``view_display( )`` and ``message_toast_display( )`` receive; a test then` && |\n| &&
             `  calls ``main( )`` and asserts.` && |\n| &&
             `  [abap2UI5/app-template](https://github.com/abap2UI5/app-template) ships` && |\n| &&
             `  one for its starter class - abaplint checks it statically, ABAP Unit runs` && |\n| &&
             `  it on the system, and the MCP server's ``run_unit_tests`` runs it in the` && |\n| &&
             `  transpiled backend; ``npm run test:unit`` in the project and the` && |\n| &&
             `  ``abap2UI5/mcp-server`` GitHub Action do the same at the terminal and in CI,` && |\n| &&
             `  no system involved. Implement every method the app calls in the double:` && |\n| &&
             `  the transpiled runtime generates no empty stubs for a ``PARTIALLY` && |\n| &&
             `  IMPLEMENTED`` interface, a system does.` && |\n| &&
             `- **``npm run doctor``** in a project made from app-template: the environment` && |\n| &&
             `  check - Node, the two gates, Chromium for the render gate, the framework` && |\n| &&
             `  pin, the sidecars - that names the remedy for each failure.` && |\n| &&
             `- **``npm create abap2ui5-app@latest my-app -- --class zcl_my_app``**: the` && |\n| &&
             `  project scaffold without a GitHub template button or an editor.` && |\n| &&
             `- **``interact_app``** in the MCP server: click, type and fire events in the` && |\n| &&
             `  headless app and look at the result - the event branch, not just the boot.` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `## 10. The in-app developer tools (Ctrl+F12)` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `Every abap2UI5 page carries its own developer tools: a dialog over the running` && |\n| &&
             `app that shows the roundtrips, the view XML and the model, the log and the` && |\n| &&
             `environment, without the browser's devtools. They are part of the frontend` && |\n| &&
             `(``app/webapp/devtools/``), so they are there on every system and in every` && |\n| &&
             `app, with nothing to install and nothing to configure.` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `### Starting them` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `| How | What it does |` && |\n| &&
             `|---|---|` && |\n| &&
             `| **Ctrl+F12** in the running app | Opens the dialog; Ctrl+F12 again closes it. Without a tab named, it reopen` &&
             `s where you left off (remembered per browser tab in ``sessionStorage``) |` && |\n| &&
             `| **``?z2ui5-devtools=1``** on the page URL | Opens the tools as soon as the page has booted, on the Overview. F` &&
             `or a problem that happens during startup, where Ctrl+F12 comes too late. Example: ``https://<host>/sap/bc/z2ui5` &&
             `?sap-client=100&z2ui5-devtools=1`` |` && |\n| &&
             `| **``?z2ui5-devtools=<KEY>``** | Opens them directly on one view, by its key. Group keys: ``OVERVIEW``, ``PROBLEMS` &&
             ```, ``ROUNDTRIPS``, ``VIEWDATA``, ``SYSTEM``, ``SEARCH``. View keys: ``ERROR``, ``LOG``, ``HISTORY``, ``REQUEST``, ``PLAIN``, ``AC` &&
             `TIONS``, ``DIFF``, ``VIEWDIFF``, ``VIEW``, ``MODEL``, ``BINDINGS``, ``POPUP``, ``POPUP_MODEL``, ``POPUP_BINDINGS``, ``POPOVER``, ` &&
             ```POPOVER_MODEL``, ``POPOVER_BINDINGS``, ``NEST1``, ``NEST2``, ``JOURNEY``. Example: ``?z2ui5-devtools=HISTORY`` |` && |\n| &&
             `| **"Open on Error"** switch on the Overview tab | Once on, the tools pop open on the Log as soon as anything ` &&
             `logs at error level: a backend error, an uncaught exception, an unhandled rejection, a binding problem. Off by` &&
             ` default, remembered per browser tab |` && |\n| &&
             `| From the **start app** (``z2ui5_cl_ui5_app_start``) | The System information popup covers the backend (setting` &&
             `s, user exit, drafts); its text points to Ctrl+F12 for the frontend side (UI5 version, theme, device, requests` &&
             `, logs) |` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `The roundtrip history and the console capture record from the first` && |\n| &&
             `roundtrip on, whether the dialog was ever opened or not: opening the tools` && |\n| &&
             `after the problem still shows what happened before. The dialog itself and` && |\n| &&
             `the inspectors arrive on the first Ctrl+F12 as a second bundle` && |\n| &&
             `(``GET <page url>&z2ui5-bundle=devtools``, cached by ETag), so a plain app` && |\n| &&
             `start does not pay for them. There is no backend switch and no ABAP call to` && |\n| &&
             `open them; they are a frontend affair.` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `### What you find there` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `- **Overview**: which app, which roundtrip, is anything broken, and where to` && |\n| &&
             `  go next. The landing tab, with the "Open on Error" switch.` && |\n| &&
             `- **Problems**: the last fatal error (with Retry / Restart / Logout) and one` && |\n| &&
             `  Log timeline of everything: the framework's error log with stack traces,` && |\n| &&
             `  UI5's log, uncaught errors, rejections, every ``console.*`` call and the` && |\n| &&
             `  messages the user was shown.` && |\n| &&
             `- **Roundtrips**: every roundtrip with backend vs. render time, payload sizes` && |\n| &&
             `  and draft ids, the raw request and response JSON, the follow-up actions and` && |\n| &&
             `  a diff of the model between two roundtrips. The **Journey** view records a` && |\n| &&
             `  click-through: press "Record Journey", use the app, press it again, and` && |\n| &&
             `  "Export ABAP Unit" hands over a local test class that replays the steps on` && |\n| &&
             `  ``z2ui5_cl_frontend_simulator`` ([headless-frontend](https://github.com/abap2UI5/headless-frontend))` && |\n| &&
             `  - ``set_value( )`` for what was typed, ``click( )`` for every event, assertions` && |\n| &&
             `  on the messages, layers, control ids and events the screens showed. Paste it` && |\n| &&
             `  into the app's test include; record from the app start, because the test` && |\n| &&
             `  starts the app fresh.` && |\n| &&
             `- **View & Data**: the XML of the main view, the popup, the popover and the` && |\n| &&
             `  nested views as the backend sent it, the model that fills each, and the` && |\n| &&
             `  bindings with a missing-path check and a size ranking. The picker marks a` && |\n| &&
             `  control on screen and jumps to its XML.` && |\n| &&
             `- **System**: UI5 version, theme, device, the running app's ABAP class.` && |\n| &&
             `- **Search**: one term across every other tab at once.` && |\n| &&
             `- **Report a Bug** (toolbar): puts the whole session state on the clipboard as a` && |\n| &&
             `  GitHub-ready issue body (environment, error, log, roundtrip history, the` && |\n| &&
             `  app's class, each in a collapsed section). Paste it into an issue as it is.` && |\n| &&
             `- The **(i)** button opens the built-in help with the same keys and shortcuts.` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `### When they do not open` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `- The page runs under the shipped CSP; the devtools bundle is a same-origin` && |\n| &&
             `  file and needs nothing beyond ``script-src 'self'``. A CSP of your own that` && |\n| &&
             `  drops ``'self'`` blocks it, and the Log of the browser's console names the` && |\n| &&
             `  blocked URL.` && |\n| &&
             `- On a Fiori launchpad or a BSP page the dialog's modules are asked from the` && |\n| &&
             `  page's own loader first and from the bundle second; a 404 in between is` && |\n| &&
             `  expected and harmless.` && |\n| &&
             `- An embedded component (``@abap2ui5/embed-control``, ``?z2ui5-bundle``) has the` && |\n| &&
             `  tools too, loaded from its own backend endpoint, but without the page-wide` && |\n| &&
             `  console capture: the host's page is not the app's.` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `## 11. Calling a language model` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             ```z2ui5_if_ui5_llm`` is the one seam: ``chat( system t_message s_options )``` && |\n| &&
             `takes a system prompt, the conversation (``role`` ``user``/``assistant`` plus` && |\n| &&
             ```content``) and model/``max_tokens``/``temperature``, and answers ``text``,` && |\n| &&
             ```stop_reason`` and ``s_usage``; every failure is ``z2ui5_cx_ui5_llm`` (``get_text( )``` && |\n| &&
             `for the user, ``retryable`` for a 408/429/5xx or a timeout). Get a provider from` && |\n| &&
             ```z2ui5_cl_ui5_llm``: ``create_claude( )`` (Messages API), ``create_openai( )``` && |\n| &&
             `(Chat Completions - OpenAI, Azure with ``auth_header`` set to ``api-key``, Ollama,` && |\n| &&
             `LM Studio, gateways) or ``create_local( t_rule = ... )``, a deterministic` && |\n| &&
             `rule-based provider without HTTP for 7.02, unit tests and demos.` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             ```````abap` && |\n| &&
             `DATA(li_llm) = z2ui5_cl_ui5_llm=>create_claude( model       = ls_cfg-model` && |\n| &&
             `                                                destination = ls_cfg-destination ).` && |\n| &&
             `DATA(ls_answer) = li_llm->chat( system    = ``Answer briefly.``` && |\n| &&
             `                                t_message = mt_chat ).` && |\n| &&
             ```````` && |\n| &&
             |\n| &&
             `- **No key, model or endpoint in the class.** Read them from your own` && |\n| &&
             `  configuration and pass a destination (SM59 on Standard, a communication` && |\n| &&
             `  arrangement or BTP destination on Cloud) or a URL plus key; there is no` && |\n| &&
             `  default model.` && |\n| &&
             `- Create the provider in the method that calls it - never keep it in an` && |\n| &&
             `  attribute, the app instance is serialized every roundtrip. Keep the` && |\n| &&
             `  conversation (``mt_chat``) as the attribute instead, and call in an event` && |\n| &&
             `  branch: the user waits for the whole answer.` && |\n| &&
             ``.

  ENDMETHOD.

ENDCLASS.
